$\begin{align}
\dfrac{5^{10}}{5^3}&=5^{10-3}
\\\\
&=5^7
\end{align}$

This follows from the general rule $\dfrac{x^m}{x^n}=x^{m-n}$. Note that the powers have the same base.

We can also see this is correct by expanding the powers.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{5^{10}}{5^3}&=\dfrac{\overbrace{\cancel 5\cdot \cancel 5\cdot \cancel 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5}^\text{10 times}}{\underbrace{\cancel 5\cdot \cancel 5\cdot \cancel 5}_\text{3 times}}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5\cdot 5}_\text{7 times}
\\\\
&=5^7
\end{align}$
